a preschool animation broadcast on Channel 5, featuring handcrafted puppets and gentle storytelling.\",\"uploadDate\":\"2018-09-24T00:00:00+00:00\"}"}}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Becca’s Bunch Voiceover – Ringo the Turtle"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-sub","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<p>\r\nIn 2018, I voiced Ringo the turtle in <em>Becca’s Bunch</em>, a preschool animation series featuring handcrafted puppet characters and gentle, character-led storytelling.\r\n</p>"}}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-post-body","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-main two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Voicing Ringo in Becca’s Bunch</h2>\r\n<p>\r\n<em>Becca’s Bunch</em> is a preschool television series that originally aired on Channel 5 in the UK. The show follows Becca and her group of friends as they explore everyday adventures in Wagtail Woods, with a strong focus on kindness, curiosity and problem-solving.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nRingo is a friendly turtle who works as a bus driver, often popping up throughout the series as a familiar and reassuring presence. Although the show hasn’t been recommissioned for further series, there were a substantial number of episodes produced, and Ringo appeared regularly across them.\r\n</p>"}}],false,["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"embed-wrap","children":["$","iframe",null,{"src":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/HeWhEx_QAh0","title":"Becca’s Bunch Voiceover – Ringo the Turtle","allow":"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture","allowFullScreen":true}]}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/beccas-bunce-voice-of-ringo.jpg","alt":"Becca’s Bunch Voiceover – Ringo the Turtle Character","className":"blog-post-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Character Voiceover for Children’s Television</h2>\r\n<p>\r\nVoicing characters for children’s television requires a balance of warmth, clarity and personality. Ringo’s voice needed to feel friendly and dependable, without overpowering the gentle tone of the series.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nThis kind of work sits firmly within my <a href=\"/https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/character-voiceover\">character voiceover</a> work, alongside other long-running children’s TV projects.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nI’ve also voiced multiple characters in <em>Thomas &amp; Friends</em>, including Winston, Salty and Troublesome Tanker 2, roles that similarly rely on clear characterisation and consistent delivery across episodes. You can read more about that work on my <a href=\"/https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/thomas-the-tank-engine-voice-of-winston\">Thomas &amp; Friends voiceover page</a>.\r\n</p>"}}]]}],[],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-bottom-text","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Looking for a Character Voice?</h2>\r\n<p>\r\nIf you’re producing animation, children’s content or character-led projects and need a reliable, experienced voice, I’m always happy to chat.\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nYou can get in touch directly via my <a href=\"/https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/contact-guy\">contact page</a>.\r\n</p>"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-cta","children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/voiceover-news","className":"cta-btn cta-btn--outline","children":"← Back to News & Blog"}]}],["$","$L4",null,{"pageTitle":"Becca’s Bunch Voiceover – Ringo the Turtle","pageUrl":"beccas-bunce-voice-of-ringo"}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-related-strip","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":["$","div",nul